// The Feud — Hag first talk (snake venom request) + no-snake re-talk +
// snake-basket handover. New file.
// CANDIDATE 2007-base (OSRS Transcript:The Feud § Talking to Ali the Hag /
// Talking to Ali the Hag again / with a Snake basket full, dump §15.3 +
// §15.4 + §15.6). NPC feud_hag 1871 @ 3346,2987 L0, display Ali the Hag.
// Gate: %feud_found_trait >= 1 (traitor report) else return — the dump has
// no pre-tree here. First tree verbatim: "Good day, Hag." / "Blockhead" /
// "remove someone" / 'Traitorous Ali', please -> pickled aubergines ->
// "bring me some snake venom" through "...that snake charmer's pet worm,
// it's about as dangerous as a rubber knife." First tree ends with
// %feud_var_witchbothered = 1 (CANDIDATE — picked over %feud_hag_list).
// Re-talk when witchbothered >= 1 and no basket_with_snake held (dump
// §15.4): "Have you got a snake yet?" / "No, I'm still working on that." /
// "Well don't bother me again until you do!" Have-snake when witchbothered
// >= 1 and basket_with_snake 4607 held (dump §15.6): verbatim through
// "Oops! I almost forgot!" + mes "You hand the basket with the charmed
// snake over to the old hag." + inv_del basket_with_snake 4607, then
// %feud_hag_list = 1 (CANDIDATE — ingredients / snake delivered). No-dung
// re-talk when hag_list >= 1 and no feud_camel_pooh_bucket and no
// feud_camel_poison_pooh_bucket held (dump §15.7): "Do you have the camel
// dung yet?" / "No, I'm still working on that." / "Well don't come back
// until you have it!" Have-dung when hag_list >= 1 and feud_camel_pooh_bucket
// 4601 held (dump §15.8): verbatim through "Got it. Thanks again!" + mes
// "You hand over your bucket of fresh camel dung and receive a vial of
// poison in return." + inv_del feud_camel_pooh_bucket 4601, then
// inv_add poison_from_hag 4604. Stage/count stay. No 28. No dest / p_tele.
// Table poison Use (§16.2) is later. No && / ||.
// Cite feud-config-unit-first-377.md · osrs-wiki-changes-crawl-377.md.

[opnpc1,feud_hag]
if (%feud_found_trait < 1) { return; }
if (%feud_var_witchbothered >= 1 & inv_total(inv, basket_with_snake) >= 1) {
    @feud_hag_have_snake;
}
if (%feud_hag_list >= 1 & inv_total(inv, feud_camel_pooh_bucket) >= 1) {
    @feud_hag_have_dung;
}
if (%feud_hag_list >= 1 & inv_total(inv, feud_camel_pooh_bucket) < 1 & inv_total(inv, feud_camel_poison_pooh_bucket) < 1) {
    @feud_hag_no_dung;
}
if (%feud_var_witchbothered >= 1 & inv_total(inv, basket_with_snake) < 1) {
    @feud_hag_no_snake;
}
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>Good day, Hag.");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Good day to you too, Blockhead.");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Now what do you want? A hex? A spot potion? Power, beauty, eternal youth, etcetera?");
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>Actually I just want your help to, erm, remove someone. It's simple enough!");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Ahh, I see. But I warn you, stranger - extinguishing the flame of life is simple, but people rarely wish to face the consequences, and I doubt you are any different.");
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>Don't worry about the consequences - I need it carried out in a manner which would draw no suspicion to me.");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Well now this is getting interesting. I'd recommend a poisoning. Who do you wish dead? I need to know so that I may tailor a poison to their specific needs.");
~chatplayer("<p,quiz>'Traitorous Ali', please.");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Traitorous Ali? Say no more! That wretch traded his grandmother's house for a jar of pickled aubergines! I believe he'll be easily gotten rid of...");
~chatplayer("<p,quiz>What payment do you require?");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>None at all - I will extract much pleasure from his passing. Just bring me the ingredients I require.");
~chatplayer("<p,quiz>What do you need?");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Ah, impatience! Traitorous Ali's time is indeed nigh. Firstly bring me some snake venom, which will act as the main toxin.");
~chatplayer("<p,quiz>Where would I get some snake poison?");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>From a snake perhaps?");
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>What I meant was how do I extract the poison from the snake?");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Sheesh! You'd make a terrible hag. Just bring me a snake with teeth in its head - and don't even think of giving me that snake charmer's pet worm, it's about as dangerous as a rubber knife.");
%feud_var_witchbothered = 1; // CANDIDATE — first talk done; opens the §15.4 re-talk
return;

[label,feud_hag_no_snake]
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>Good day, Hag.");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Good day to you too, Blockhead.");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Have you got a snake yet?");
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>No, I'm still working on that.");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Well don't bother me again until you do!");
return;

[label,feud_hag_have_snake]
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>Good day, Hag.");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Good day to you too, Blockhead.");
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>I have the snake. What else do you need?");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Ah yes, that snake will do nicely. Hello, you wriggly little cutie!");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Who's a vindictive little beast? You are! You are!");
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>Erm, yes. Do you need anything else?");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Now that I have the toxin I need something to hide its trace. Fresh camel dung should do the job.");
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>What? That's disgusting.");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Do you want the poison or not?");
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>Fine, fine, I'll get some camel dung.");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>And make that fresh camel dung! Nice and stinky. Now hand over that venomous little darling before it takes a bite out of you.");
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>Oops! I almost forgot!");
mes("You hand the basket with the charmed snake over to the old hag.");
inv_del(inv, basket_with_snake, 1);
%feud_hag_list = 1; // CANDIDATE — snake delivered; opens the §15.7 dung-wait re-talk
return;

[label,feud_hag_no_dung]
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>Good day, Hag.");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Good day to you too, Blockhead.");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Do you have the camel dung yet?");
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>No, I'm still working on that.");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Well don't come back until you have it!");
return;

[label,feud_hag_have_dung]
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>Good day, Hag.");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Good day to you too, Blockhead.");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Here's your poison!");
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>Wow, that was quick!");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Actually I already had it brewing. I just needed the ingredients for another batch.");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>You wouldn't believe the demand. It's been murder!");
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>That's not even remotely funny.");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Sorry, I've been dying to say that for ages.");
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>Just stop. Thanks for the poison and good day to you.");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Wait! Just remember, this poison isn't designed to be used on a weapon. In fact it's not a contact poison at all. You'll have to do more than just smear it on a blade!");
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>Got it. Thanks again!");
mes("You hand over your bucket of fresh camel dung and receive a vial of poison in return.");
inv_del(inv, feud_camel_pooh_bucket, 1);
inv_add(inv, poison_from_hag, 1);
return;
